window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["graphql"]=[{"id":"graphql-f0001","card":"q-graphql-001-1-what-graphql-is-and-why","sec":"graphql-s002","q":"What is GraphQL?","a":"<p>A <strong>query language for APIs</strong>. It is not a database and not a client. It acts as a server-side layer that sits in front of data stores.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0002","card":"q-graphql-001-1-what-graphql-is-and-why","sec":"graphql-s002","q":"Why was GraphQL created at Meta (Facebook)?","a":"<p>REST could not handle deep queries (4-5 levels deep in a friend network). GraphQL handles any depth across multiple databases.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0003","card":"q-graphql-001-1-what-graphql-is-and-why","sec":"graphql-s002","q":"Which implementations make up the GraphQL ecosystem?","a":"<p>Facebook's reference implementation, Apollo and Relay.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0004","card":"q-graphql-001-1-what-graphql-is-and-why","sec":"graphql-s002","q":"What are the main benefits of GraphQL?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Benefit</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Precise fetching</td><td>Client asks for exactly the fields it wants, so there is no over-fetching</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Type checking</td><td>The schema describes and enforces types (like TypeScript)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Multiple data stores</td><td>One request can pull from several databases</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Single entry point</td><td>All input is validated by the schema before it reaches the database</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0005","card":"q-graphql-001-1-what-graphql-is-and-why","sec":"graphql-s002","q":"How does a REST call differ from a GraphQL query for user data?","a":"<p>REST returns all user fields (over-fetching). GraphQL returns only the fields you ask for.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>REST:     GET /users                    -&gt; returns ALL user fields (over-fetching)\nGraphQL:  query { user { name email } } -&gt; returns ONLY name and email</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0006","card":"q-graphql-001-1-what-graphql-is-and-why","sec":"graphql-s002","q":"What happens when you send a Boolean (<code>name: true</code>) for a <code>String</code> field in GraphQL?","a":"<p>GraphQL rejects it, and the database is never reached.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0007","card":"q-graphql-001-1-what-graphql-is-and-why","sec":"graphql-s002","q":"Which editor tooling helps with GraphQL?","a":"<p>VS Code with a GraphQL extension (general GraphQL, Apollo GraphQL, or Relay variants). WebStorm has built-in support.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0008","card":"q-graphql-002-2-project-and-server-setup","sec":"graphql-s003","q":"Which npm packages does the GraphQL project install at runtime and for dev?","a":"<p>Runtime: <code>express</code>, <code>express-graphql</code>, <code>graphql</code> and <code>nodemon</code>. Dev: Babel packages for ES module syntax (<code>import</code>/<code>export</code>).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>npm install express express-graphql graphql nodemon\nnpm install --save-dev @babel/cli @babel/core @babel/node @babel/preset-env</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0009","card":"q-graphql-002-2-project-and-server-setup","sec":"graphql-s003","q":"What does each package do in the GraphQL server project?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>express</code></td><td>Web server</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>express-graphql</code></td><td>GraphQL middleware for Express (<code>graphqlHTTP</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>graphql</code></td><td>Core GraphQL library (<code>buildSchema</code>)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>nodemon</code></td><td>Restarts the server on file change (type <code>rs</code> to restart manually)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>@babel/*</code></td><td>Lets Node run <code>import</code>/<code>export</code> syntax</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0010","card":"q-graphql-002-2-project-and-server-setup","sec":"graphql-s003","q":"What goes in <code>.babelrc</code> for the GraphQL project?","a":"<p>The <code>@babel/preset-env</code> preset.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{\n    &quot;presets&quot;: [\n        &quot;@babel/preset-env&quot;\n    ]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0011","card":"q-graphql-002-2-project-and-server-setup","sec":"graphql-s003","q":"How does the <code>start</code> script run the server?","a":"<p><code>--exec babel-node</code> compiles ES modules first, and <code>-e js</code> watches <code>.js</code> files.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;scripts&quot;: {\n    &quot;start&quot;: &quot;nodemon ./index.js --exec babel-node -e js&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0012","card":"q-graphql-002-2-project-and-server-setup","sec":"graphql-s003","q":"What does the base Express <code>index.js</code> look like, and on which port does it run?","a":"<p>It serves on <code>localhost:8080</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import express from &#x27;express&#x27;;\n\nconst PORT = 8080;\nconst app = express();\n\napp.get(&#x27;/&#x27;, (req, res) =&gt; {\n    res.send(&#x27;GraphQL is amazing!&#x27;);\n});\n\napp.listen(PORT, () =&gt; console.log(`Running server on localhost:${PORT}/graphql`));</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0013","card":"q-graphql-002-2-project-and-server-setup","sec":"graphql-s003","q":"How do you start the GraphQL server?","a":"<p>Run <code>npm start</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>npm start</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0014","card":"q-graphql-003-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"Schema vs resolver in GraphQL?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>Schema</th><th>Resolver</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Defines</td><td><strong>What</strong> types and queries exist (blueprint/contract)</td><td><strong>How</strong> the data is returned (implementation)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Contains</td><td>Type definitions only, no logic</td><td>Functions that return data</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>File</td><td><code>data/schema.js</code></td><td><code>index.js</code> (<code>rootValue</code>), later <code>data/resolvers.js</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0015","card":"q-graphql-003-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"What two rules apply to every GraphQL schema and its resolvers?","a":"<p>Every schema must have <code>type Query</code> listing all queryable fields. Resolver function names must exactly match the schema's query/mutation field names.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0016","card":"q-graphql-003-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"What is the flow of a GraphQL request?","a":"<p>Client query, then the schema validates types, then the resolver returns data.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0017","card":"q-graphql-003-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"What does a Hello World GraphQL schema look like?","a":"<p>It uses <code>buildSchema</code> with a <code>Query</code> type that has one <code>String</code> field.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import { buildSchema } from &#x27;graphql&#x27;;\n\nconst schema = buildSchema(`\n    type Query {\n        hello: String\n    }\n`);\n\nexport default schema;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0018","card":"q-graphql-003-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"How do you wire a schema and resolver into Express?","a":"<p>Mount <code>graphqlHTTP</code> at <code>/graphql</code> with <code>schema</code>, <code>rootValue</code> and <code>graphiql</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>const root = { hello: () =&gt; &quot;Hi, I&#x27;m Manny!&quot; };\n\napp.use(&#x27;/graphql&#x27;, graphqlHTTP({\n    schema: schema,\n    rootValue: root,\n    graphiql: true,\n}));</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0019","card":"q-graphql-003-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"What do the <code>graphqlHTTP</code> options <code>schema</code>, <code>rootValue</code> and <code>graphiql</code> do?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>schema</code></td><td>The schema blueprint</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>rootValue</code></td><td>Object of resolver functions, matched to fields by name</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>graphiql</code></td><td><code>true</code> serves the GraphiQL browser IDE at <code>/graphql</code> (its Docs panel is built from the schema)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0020","card":"q-graphql-003-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"How do you test the <code>hello</code> query and what is the result?","a":"<p>Run it at <code>localhost:8080/graphql</code>. The result is a JSON <code>data</code> object.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{\n    hello\n}</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{\n    &quot;data&quot;: {\n        &quot;hello&quot;: &quot;Hi, I&#x27;m Manny!&quot;\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0021","card":"q-graphql-004-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"How do you define a custom <code>Product</code> type and query it in GraphQL?","a":"<p>Declare the object type and return it from <code>Query</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>const schema = buildSchema(`\n    type Product {\n        id: ID\n        name: String\n        description: String\n        price: Float\n        soldout: Boolean\n    }\n\n    type Query {\n        product: Product\n    }\n`);</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0022","card":"q-graphql-004-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"What does a resolver with fake data look like?","a":"<p>It returns an object matching the type. A real app would call a database here.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>const root = {\n    product: () =&gt; {\n        return {\n            &quot;id&quot;: 29729872,\n            &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Widget&quot;,\n            &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Beautiful widget to use in the garden&quot;,\n            &quot;price&quot;: 34.99,\n            &quot;soldout&quot;: false\n        }\n    }\n};</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0023","card":"q-graphql-004-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"How do you query every field of <code>product</code>?","a":"<p>List the fields in the selection.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query {\n    product {\n        id\n        name\n        description\n        price\n        soldout\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0024","card":"q-graphql-004-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"How is <code>id</code> returned in the <code>product</code> response?","a":"<p>As a string, <code>\"id\": \"29729872\"</code>, because <code>ID</code> is serialized as a String.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0025","card":"q-graphql-004-3-schema-and-resolvers","sec":"graphql-s004","q":"What happens if you ask for only <code>name description price</code>?","a":"<p>Only those fields come back, so there is no over-fetching.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0026","card":"q-graphql-005-scalars-built-in-no-definition-needed","sec":"graphql-s005","q":"What are the built-in GraphQL scalar types?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>Int</code></td><td>Whole number</td><td><code>42</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>Float</code></td><td>Decimal</td><td><code>34.99</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>String</code></td><td>Text</td><td><code>\"Widget\"</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>Boolean</code></td><td>true/false</td><td><code>false</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>ID</code></td><td>Unique identifier (serialized as a String)</td><td><code>\"29729872\"</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0027","card":"q-graphql-005-scalars-built-in-no-definition-needed","sec":"graphql-s005","q":"Do you need to define the GraphQL scalar types?","a":"<p>No. They are built in.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0028","card":"q-graphql-006-object-types-lists-non-null","sec":"graphql-s006","q":"What is an object type in GraphQL, and what does <code>[Store]</code> mean?","a":"<p>An object type groups fields into a shape. <code>[Store]</code> is a list of <code>Store</code> objects.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0029","card":"q-graphql-006-object-types-lists-non-null","sec":"graphql-s006","q":"What does <code>!</code> mean, and what does <code>[Store]!</code> require?","a":"<p><code>!</code> means non-null. In <code>[Store]!</code> it applies to the list itself, so the list must be present (an empty array is fine), not to the items.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0030","card":"q-graphql-006-object-types-lists-non-null","sec":"graphql-s006","q":"What do <code>[Store]</code>, <code>[Store]!</code> and <code>ID!</code> mean?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Syntax</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>[Store]</code></td><td>Optional list of Store objects</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>[Store]!</code></td><td>List must be present</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>ID!</code></td><td>Required scalar</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0031","card":"q-graphql-006-object-types-lists-non-null","sec":"graphql-s006","q":"How do you add a nested <code>Store</code> list to <code>Product</code> in the schema?","a":"<p>Add a <code>stores: [Store]!</code> field and define the <code>Store</code> type.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>stores: [Store]!\ntype Store {\n    store: String\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0032","card":"q-graphql-006-object-types-lists-non-null","sec":"graphql-s006","q":"How does a resolver return nested stores?","a":"<p>As an array of objects.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;stores&quot;: [\n    { store: &quot;Pasadena&quot; },\n    { store: &quot;Los Angeles&quot; }\n]</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0033","card":"q-graphql-006-object-types-lists-non-null","sec":"graphql-s006","q":"How do you query nested store names?","a":"<p>Select the nested field inside <code>product</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query {\n    product {\n        name\n        price\n        stores {\n            store\n        }\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0034","card":"q-graphql-007-query-vs-mutation","sec":"graphql-s007","q":"Query vs Mutation in GraphQL?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>SQL analogy</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>type Query</code></td><td>Read data</td><td><code>SELECT</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>type Mutation</code></td><td>Create, update, delete</td><td><code>INSERT</code>, <code>UPDATE</code>, <code>DELETE</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0035","card":"q-graphql-008-input-types","sec":"graphql-s008","q":"Which GraphQL keyword declares object arguments for a mutation?","a":"<p><strong><code>input</code></strong>, not <code>type</code>. <code>type</code> is for output shapes, <code>input</code> is for argument shapes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0036","card":"q-graphql-008-input-types","sec":"graphql-s008","q":"What must match between a <code>type</code> and its <code>input</code>?","a":"<p>Every <code>type</code> field you want to send via a mutation must exist in the matching <code>input</code>. Lists need a matching input type (<code>[Store]!</code> becomes <code>[StoreInput]!</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0037","card":"q-graphql-008-input-types","sec":"graphql-s008","q":"What error appears if you declare mutation arguments with <code>type</code> instead of <code>input</code>?","a":"<p>A runtime error, and the fix is to change both to <code>input</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>The type of mutation createProduct input must be input type but got ProductInput</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0038","card":"q-graphql-008-input-types","sec":"graphql-s008","q":"What does the corrected schema with a <code>createProduct</code> mutation and a <code>getProduct(id)</code> query look like?","a":"<p>It has <code>Query</code>, <code>input</code> types and <code>Mutation</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>type Query {\n    getProduct(id: ID): Product\n}\n\ninput StoreInput {\n    store: String\n}\n\ntype Mutation {\n    createProduct(input: ProductInput): Product\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0039","card":"q-graphql-009-adding-a-scalar-field-inventory-int","sec":"graphql-s009","q":"In how many places do you update the code to add a field such as <code>inventory: Int</code>?","a":"<p>Three places: the output <code>type Product</code>, the <code>input ProductInput</code>, and the <code>Product</code> class constructor in the resolvers (in-memory phase; with MongoDB the Mongoose schema replaces the class).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0040","card":"q-graphql-009-adding-a-scalar-field-inventory-int","sec":"graphql-s009","q":"How is <code>inventory: Int</code> added to the <code>Product</code> schema type and input?","a":"<p>As a field in both the output type and the input.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>inventory: Int\nstores: [Store]!</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0041","card":"q-graphql-009-adding-a-scalar-field-inventory-int","sec":"graphql-s009","q":"How does the <code>Product</code> class constructor handle <code>inventory</code>?","a":"<p>It destructures it and assigns it.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>constructor(id, { name, description, price, soldout, inventory, stores }) {\n    this.inventory = inventory;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0042","card":"q-graphql-010-enums","sec":"graphql-s010","q":"What is a GraphQL enum, and why use it instead of a Boolean?","a":"<p>An enum restricts a field to a fixed set of named values. It is more descriptive and extensible than a Boolean. Values are <code>ALL_CAPS</code> by convention.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0043","card":"q-graphql-010-enums","sec":"graphql-s010","q":"How does <code>soldout: Boolean</code> become an enum?","a":"<p>Declare the enum and use it in both the type and the input.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>enum Soldout {\n    SOLDOUT\n    ONSALE\n}\nsoldout: Soldout</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0044","card":"q-graphql-010-enums","sec":"graphql-s010","q":"Why is switching Boolean to an enum a breaking change?","a":"<p>Old values fail with an error.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Enum &quot;Soldout&quot; cannot represent non-enum value: false</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0045","card":"q-graphql-010-enums","sec":"graphql-s010","q":"How do you write the old Boolean values with the <code>Soldout</code> enum?","a":"<p>Use <code>soldout: ONSALE</code> (was <code>false</code>) or <code>soldout: SOLDOUT</code> (was <code>true</code>), unquoted.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0046","card":"q-graphql-010-enums","sec":"graphql-s010","q":"What should you do after a schema change, and how is the enum returned?","a":"<p>Restart the server (<code>rs</code>) and refresh GraphiQL. The response returns the enum as a string (<code>\"soldout\": \"ONSALE\"</code>).</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0047","card":"q-graphql-011-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"What does the in-memory <code>Product</code> class and database look like?","a":"<p>A <code>Product</code> class plus a plain object as a database, lost on every restart.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>const productDatabase = {};   // in-memory store</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0048","card":"q-graphql-011-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"What do the in-memory <code>getProduct</code> and <code>createProduct</code> resolvers do?","a":"<p><code>getProduct</code> builds a <code>Product</code> from the stored input. <code>createProduct</code> generates an id, stores the input and returns the new <code>Product</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>getProduct: ({ id }) =&gt; {\n    return new Product(id, productDatabase[id]);\n},\ncreateProduct: ({ input }) =&gt; {\n    let id = require(&#x27;crypto&#x27;).randomBytes(10).toString(&#x27;hex&#x27;);\n    productDatabase[id] = input;\n    return new Product(id, input);\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0049","card":"q-graphql-011-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"What does <code>{ input }</code> mean in <code>createProduct: ({ input })</code>?","a":"<p>It destructures the <code>input</code> argument.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0050","card":"q-graphql-011-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"How does the course generate a unique id for a new product?","a":"<p><code>crypto.randomBytes(10).toString('hex')</code>.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0051","card":"q-graphql-011-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"What bug did the course hit before extracting resolvers?","a":"<p>The inline resolver was misspelled <code>creatProduct</code>, and the query was named <code>product</code>. After extraction they became <code>createProduct</code> and <code>getProduct</code>, matching the schema names.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0052","card":"q-graphql-011-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"Why extract resolvers into <code>data/resolvers.js</code>?","a":"<p>It keeps <code>index.js</code> small and separates concerns. An inline <code>root</code> is fine only for tiny prototypes.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0053","card":"q-graphql-012-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"How does the clean <code>index.js</code> use the extracted resolvers?","a":"<p>It imports <code>resolvers</code> and passes them as <code>rootValue</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import resolvers from &#x27;./data/resolvers&#x27;;\nrootValue: resolvers,</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0054","card":"q-graphql-012-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"What is the GraphQL project folder layout?","a":"<p><code>data/schema.js</code> holds types, queries and mutations. <code>data/resolvers.js</code> holds the Product class, database and resolver functions. Alongside are <code>.babelrc</code>, <code>index.js</code> (the Express server) and <code>package.json</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>├── data/\n│   ├── schema.js       types, queries, mutations\n│   └── resolvers.js    Product class + database + resolver functions\n├── .babelrc\n├── index.js            Express server\n└── package.json</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0055","card":"q-graphql-012-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"How do you run a <code>createProduct</code> mutation?","a":"<p>Use the <code>mutation</code> keyword with an <code>input</code> object and select the returned fields.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>mutation {\n    createProduct(input: {\n        name: &quot;New Widget&quot;,\n        description: &quot;A brand new widget&quot;,\n        price: 19.99,\n        soldout: false,\n        stores: [{ store: &quot;New York&quot; }]\n    }) {\n        id\n        name\n        price\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0056","card":"q-graphql-012-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"How do you fetch a product by the id returned from a mutation?","a":"<p>Call <code>getProduct</code> with the id.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query {\n    getProduct(id: &quot;&lt;paste-id-from-mutation-response&gt;&quot;) {\n        name\n        price\n        description\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0057","card":"q-graphql-012-5-mutations-with-an-in-memory-store","sec":"graphql-s011","q":"How do you test the <code>inventory</code> and enum <code>soldout: ONSALE</code> fields in a mutation?","a":"<p>Pass them in the <code>input</code>, with the enum unquoted.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>soldout: ONSALE\ninventory: 10</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0058","card":"q-graphql-013-6-persistence-mongodb-and-sqlite","sec":"graphql-s012","q":"Why move from <code>productDatabase = {}</code> to MongoDB?","a":"<p>The in-memory object is lost on restart. MongoDB (default <code>localhost:27017</code>) gives real persistence.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0059","card":"q-graphql-013-6-persistence-mongodb-and-sqlite","sec":"graphql-s012","q":"What is Robo 3T (Studio 3T) used for?","a":"<p>A GUI to verify the connection and inspect documents. Copy a document's <code>_id</code> to use in queries.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0060","card":"q-graphql-013-6-persistence-mongodb-and-sqlite","sec":"graphql-s012","q":"What is Mongoose?","a":"<p>The ODM bridging Node.js and MongoDB.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>npm install mongoose</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0061","card":"q-graphql-013-6-persistence-mongodb-and-sqlite","sec":"graphql-s012","q":"Where do DB connections and models go?","a":"<p>In a new file <code>data/dbConnectors.js</code>, which keeps <code>index.js</code> and <code>resolvers.js</code> clean. <code>index.js</code> is unchanged at this step.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0062","card":"q-graphql-013-6-persistence-mongodb-and-sqlite","sec":"graphql-s012","q":"How does <code>dbConnectors.js</code> connect to MongoDB?","a":"<p>An async function calls <code>mongoose.connect</code>, which creates the <code>widgets</code> DB if missing, and runs on file load.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>await mongoose.connect(&#x27;mongodb://localhost/widgets&#x27;);   // creates &#x27;widgets&#x27; DB if missing\nconnectMongo();   // runs on file load</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0063","card":"q-graphql-013-6-persistence-mongodb-and-sqlite","sec":"graphql-s012","q":"What is the Mongoose schema for widgets?","a":"<p>Fields with Mongoose types, registered as the <code>widgets</code> model.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>const widgetSchema = new mongoose.Schema({\n    name: String,\n    description: String,\n    price: Number,       // GraphQL Float -&gt; Mongoose Number\n    soldout: String,     // GraphQL enum -&gt; Mongoose String\n    inventory: String,   // GraphQL Int  -&gt; Mongoose String\n    stores: Array,\n});\n\nconst Widgets = mongoose.model(&#x27;widgets&#x27;, widgetSchema);</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0064","card":"q-graphql-013-6-persistence-mongodb-and-sqlite","sec":"graphql-s012","q":"GraphQL types vs Mongoose types: what is each for?","a":"<p>GraphQL types validate the API. Mongoose types control storage. They need not match exactly.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0065","card":"q-graphql-013-6-persistence-mongodb-and-sqlite","sec":"graphql-s012","q":"How do GraphQL and Mongoose types map for <code>price</code>, <code>soldout</code>, <code>inventory</code> and <code>stores</code>?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>GraphQL</th><th>Mongoose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>price</code></td><td><code>Float</code></td><td><code>Number</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>soldout</code></td><td><code>Soldout</code> enum</td><td><code>String</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>inventory</code></td><td><code>Int</code></td><td><code>String</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>stores</code></td><td><code>[Store]!</code></td><td><code>Array</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0066","card":"q-graphql-013-6-persistence-mongodb-and-sqlite","sec":"graphql-s012","q":"Why does <code>dbConnectors.js</code> use a named export?","a":"<p>The file will export several connectors, so it uses <code>export { Widgets }</code> instead of <code>export default</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import { Widgets } from &#x27;./dbConnectors&#x27;;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0067","card":"q-graphql-014-adding-sqlite-sequelize","sec":"graphql-s013","q":"Which packages add SQLite with Sequelize?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Package</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>sequelize</code></td><td>ORM for SQL databases</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>sqlite3</code></td><td>SQLite driver</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>casual</code></td><td>Fake data generator for seeding</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>lodash</code></td><td><code>_.times()</code> to repeat the seed call</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Bash</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>npm install casual lodash sequelize sqlite3</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0068","card":"q-graphql-014-adding-sqlite-sequelize","sec":"graphql-s013","q":"How do you create an in-memory SQLite database in Sequelize?","a":"<p>Pass <code>'sqlite::memory:'</code>. It lives in RAM and resets on restart.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>const sequelize = new Sequelize(&#x27;sqlite::memory:&#x27;);   // in RAM, resets on restart</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0069","card":"q-graphql-014-adding-sqlite-sequelize","sec":"graphql-s013","q":"How do you define the <code>Categories</code> model in Sequelize?","a":"<p>Use <code>sequelize.define</code> with <code>DataTypes</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>const Categories = sequelize.define(&#x27;categories&#x27;, {\n    category: DataTypes.STRING,\n    description: DataTypes.STRING,\n});</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0070","card":"q-graphql-014-adding-sqlite-sequelize","sec":"graphql-s013","q":"What does <code>sequelize.sync({ force: true })</code> do?","a":"<p>It creates the table, and drops it first if it exists.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>await sequelize.sync({ force: true });   // creates table, drops it first if it exists</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0071","card":"q-graphql-014-adding-sqlite-sequelize","sec":"graphql-s013","q":"How does the course seed fake categories?","a":"<p>It uses <code>_.times(5, ...)</code> with <code>casual</code> inside <code>Promise.all</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>await Promise.all(_.times(5, () =&gt; {\n    return Categories.create({\n        category: casual.word,\n        description: casual.sentence,\n    });\n}));</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0072","card":"q-graphql-014-adding-sqlite-sequelize","sec":"graphql-s013","q":"Mongoose vs Sequelize: how do they differ?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Concept</th><th>Mongoose</th><th>Sequelize</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>String type</td><td><code>String</code></td><td><code>DataTypes.STRING</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Number type</td><td><code>Number</code></td><td><code>DataTypes.INTEGER</code> / <code>DataTypes.FLOAT</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Define model</td><td><code>mongoose.model('name', schema)</code></td><td><code>sequelize.define('name', fields)</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Sync to DB</td><td>automatic on connect</td><td><code>sequelize.sync()</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>In-memory DB</td><td>not supported</td><td><code>'sqlite::memory:'</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0073","card":"q-graphql-014-adding-sqlite-sequelize","sec":"graphql-s013","q":"What does the server log when both connections work?","a":"<p>Three lines.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>Connected to MongoDB\nSQLite connection established and Categories model synced\nCategories seeded</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0074","card":"q-graphql-014-adding-sqlite-sequelize","sec":"graphql-s013","q":"What does the final <code>dbConnectors.js</code> export?","a":"<p>Both models.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>export { Widgets, Categories };</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0075","card":"q-graphql-015-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"What changes in the resolvers when moving to MongoDB?","a":"<p>The <code>Product</code> class and <code>productDatabase</code> are removed. Mongoose documents map directly onto the GraphQL <code>Product</code> fields. All resolvers are <code>async</code>, use <code>await</code>, and share the <code>try/catch</code> + <code>throw new Error(error)</code> pattern.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0076","card":"q-graphql-015-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"Which Mongoose method does each CRUD resolver use?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Resolver</th><th>Mongoose method</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Create</td><td><code>createProduct</code></td><td><code>new Widgets(...)</code> + <code>.save()</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Read one</td><td><code>getProduct</code></td><td><code>Widgets.findById(id)</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Read all</td><td><code>getAllProducts</code></td><td><code>Widgets.find({})</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Update</td><td><code>updateProduct</code></td><td><code>Widgets.findOneAndUpdate(filter, update, { new: true })</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Delete</td><td><code>deleteProduct</code></td><td><code>Widgets.deleteOne({ _id: id })</code></td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0077","card":"q-graphql-015-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"How does the MongoDB <code>getProduct</code> resolver work?","a":"<p>It calls <code>Widgets.findById(id)</code> and returns the product.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>getProduct: async ({ id }) =&gt; {\n    try {\n        const product = await Widgets.findById(id);\n        return product;\n    } catch (error) {\n        throw new Error(error);\n    }\n},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0078","card":"q-graphql-015-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"Why does an older document return <code>null</code> for <code>inventory</code>?","a":"<p>Documents created before <code>inventory</code> existed never stored the field.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0079","card":"q-graphql-016-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"How does the MongoDB <code>createProduct</code> resolver build the document?","a":"<p>It builds a <code>Widgets</code> document from the input. <code>new Widgets(...)</code> only builds it in memory.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>const newWidget = new Widgets({\n    name: input.name,\n    description: input.description,\n    price: input.price,\n    soldout: input.soldout,\n    inventory: input.inventory,\n    stores: input.stores,\n});</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0080","card":"q-graphql-016-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"Why does <code>createProduct</code> assign <code>newWidget.id = newWidget._id</code>?","a":"<p>MongoDB generates <code>_id</code>, and the GraphQL schema uses <code>id</code>, so the assignment bridges them.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>newWidget.id = newWidget._id;   // map MongoDB _id to GraphQL id</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0081","card":"q-graphql-016-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"How does <code>createProduct</code> persist the document?","a":"<p>It awaits <code>save()</code> and returns the widget.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>await newWidget.save();     // persist\nreturn newWidget;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0082","card":"q-graphql-016-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"How does the MongoDB <code>updateProduct</code> resolver work?","a":"<p>It reuses <code>ProductInput</code>, and its <code>id</code> locates the document.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>const updateWidget = await Widgets.findOneAndUpdate(\n    { _id: input.id },   // filter\n    input,               // new field values\n    { new: true }        // return the updated doc, not the old one\n);</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0083","card":"q-graphql-016-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"What does <code>{ new: true }</code> do in <code>findOneAndUpdate</code>?","a":"<p>It returns the updated document, not the old one. Forgetting it returns the pre-update document.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0084","card":"q-graphql-016-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"Which fields change when <code>updateProduct</code> receives only some fields?","a":"<p>Only the supplied fields change. For example, name stays unchanged and price is updated.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0085","card":"q-graphql-016-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"What must you do for every new resolver?","a":"<p>Declare it in the schema, then refresh GraphiQL so it shows in the docs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>type Mutation {\n    createProduct(input: ProductInput): Product\n    updateProduct(input: ProductInput): Product\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0086","card":"q-graphql-017-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"How does the <code>deleteProduct</code> resolver work and what does it return?","a":"<p>It takes <code>id</code> directly (not <code>input</code>) and returns a confirmation string, since there is no document left to return.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>deleteProduct: async ({ id }) =&gt; {\n    try {\n        await Widgets.deleteOne({ _id: id });\n        return &#x27;Successfully deleted widget&#x27;;\n    } catch (error) {\n        throw new Error(error);\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0087","card":"q-graphql-017-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"How is <code>deleteProduct</code> declared in the schema?","a":"<p>With a mandatory <code>ID!</code> argument and a <code>String</code> return type.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>deleteProduct(id: ID!): String</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0088","card":"q-graphql-017-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"What does <code>ID!</code> do in <code>deleteProduct(id: ID!)</code>?","a":"<p>It makes the id mandatory at the schema level.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0089","card":"q-graphql-017-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"How do you call <code>deleteProduct</code> and what is the response?","a":"<p>Run the mutation with the id.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>mutation {\n    deleteProduct(id: &quot;&lt;paste-id-here&gt;&quot;)\n}</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>{\n    &quot;data&quot;: {\n        &quot;deleteProduct&quot;: &quot;Successfully deleted widget&quot;\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0090","card":"q-graphql-017-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"Which Mongoose delete method should you use, and which is deprecated?","a":"<p>Use <code>deleteOne</code>. <code>Widgets.remove()</code> is deprecated in current Mongoose.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0091","card":"q-graphql-017-7-crud-resolvers-with-mongodb","sec":"graphql-s014","q":"Create/update vs delete: how do arguments, returns and ids differ?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th>create / update</th><th>delete</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Argument</td><td><code>input: ProductInput</code></td><td><code>id: ID!</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Returns</td><td><code>Product</code></td><td><code>String</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>id</code> needed</td><td>create: no (Mongo generates). update: yes</td><td>yes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Mongoose option</td><td>update needs <code>{ new: true }</code></td><td>n/a</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0092","card":"q-graphql-018-getallproducts","sec":"graphql-s015","q":"How does the <code>getAllProducts</code> resolver return every document?","a":"<p>It takes no arguments and uses an empty filter <code>{}</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>getAllProducts: async () =&gt; {\n    try {\n        return await Widgets.find({});\n    } catch (error) {\n        throw new Error(error);\n    }\n},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0093","card":"q-graphql-018-getallproducts","sec":"graphql-s015","q":"How is <code>getAllProducts</code> declared in the schema?","a":"<p>As a <code>Query</code> field that returns a list.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>type Query {\n    getProduct(id: ID): Product\n    getAllProducts: [Product]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0094","card":"q-graphql-018-getallproducts","sec":"graphql-s015","q":"<code>getProduct</code> vs <code>getAllProducts</code>: arguments and returns?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Query</th><th>Arguments</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><code>getProduct</code></td><td><code>id: ID</code></td><td><code>Product</code></td></tr>\n      <tr><td><code>getAllProducts</code></td><td>none</td><td><code>[Product]</code> (array)</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0095","card":"q-graphql-018-getallproducts","sec":"graphql-s015","q":"How do you query all products?","a":"<p>Select the fields you want.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query {\n    getAllProducts {\n        name\n        price\n        inventory\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0096","card":"q-graphql-019-aliases","sec":"graphql-s016","q":"What are GraphQL aliases and why use them?","a":"<p>Aliases run several queries (even the same one with different arguments) in <strong>one request</strong> and label each result. The response key is the alias, not the query name. Without aliases you would need one request per product.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0097","card":"q-graphql-019-aliases","sec":"graphql-s016","q":"Do aliases need a server change?","a":"<p>No. They are pure query syntax.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0098","card":"q-graphql-019-aliases","sec":"graphql-s016","q":"What does an aliased query for two products look like?","a":"<p>Put the alias before the query name.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query {\n    widgetone: getProduct(id: &quot;&lt;id-of-first-product&gt;&quot;) {\n        name\n        description\n        price\n    }\n    widgettwo: getProduct(id: &quot;&lt;id-of-second-product&gt;&quot;) {\n        name\n        inventory\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0099","card":"q-graphql-019-aliases","sec":"graphql-s016","q":"Can different query types be mixed in one aliased request?","a":"<p>Yes.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>query {\n    widgetone: getProduct(id: &quot;&lt;id&gt;&quot;) {\n        name\n        price\n    }\n    allItems: getAllProducts {\n        name\n        price\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0100","card":"q-graphql-020-fragments","sec":"graphql-s017","q":"What is a GraphQL fragment?","a":"<p>A reusable field selection: <code>fragment name on TypeName { fields }</code>, spread with <code>...name</code>. It is pure query syntax with no server change.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0101","card":"q-graphql-020-fragments","sec":"graphql-s017","q":"How do you define and use a fragment?","a":"<p>Define it on the type and spread it in each query.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>fragment productFragment on Product {\n    name\n    description\n    price\n}\n\nquery {\n    widgetone: getProduct(id: &quot;&lt;id-of-first-product&gt;&quot;) {\n        ...productFragment\n    }\n    allItems: getAllProducts {\n        ...productFragment\n    }\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0102","card":"q-graphql-020-fragments","sec":"graphql-s017","q":"Aliases vs fragments: when do you use each?","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Use when</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Aliases</td><td>You need several labeled results in one request</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Fragments</td><td>The same field set repeats across queries (DRY)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Both</td><td>Multiple labeled queries sharing one field set</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0103","card":"q-graphql-021-9-final-project-reference","sec":"graphql-s018","q":"What is the final GraphQL project layout?","a":"<p><code>index.js</code> is the Express server with <code>graphqlHTTP</code>. <code>data/schema.js</code> holds all type definitions, <code>data/resolvers.js</code> all CRUD resolvers, and <code>data/dbConnectors.js</code> the MongoDB and SQLite connections and models.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Text</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>├── index.js                  Express server + graphqlHTTP (see Section 5)\n└── data/\n    ├── schema.js             all type definitions\n    ├── resolvers.js          all CRUD resolvers\n    └── dbConnectors.js       MongoDB + SQLite connections and models (see Section 6)</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0104","card":"q-graphql-021-9-final-project-reference","sec":"graphql-s018","q":"What does the final <code>Product</code> type, enum and <code>Query</code> look like?","a":"<p><code>Product</code> uses the <code>Soldout</code> enum and has <code>inventory</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>type Product {\n    id: ID\n    name: String\n    description: String\n    price: Float\n    soldout: Soldout\n    inventory: Int\n    stores: [Store]!\n}\n\nenum Soldout {\n    SOLDOUT\n    ONSALE\n}\n\ntype Query {\n    getProduct(id: ID): Product\n    getAllProducts: [Product]\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0105","card":"q-graphql-021-9-final-project-reference","sec":"graphql-s018","q":"What does the final <code>Mutation</code> type declare?","a":"<p>Create, update and delete.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>type Mutation {\n    createProduct(input: ProductInput): Product\n    updateProduct(input: ProductInput): Product\n    deleteProduct(id: ID!): String\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0106","card":"q-graphql-021-9-final-project-reference","sec":"graphql-s018","q":"What is the final <code>ProductInput</code>?","a":"<p>It mirrors <code>Product</code> but uses <code>[StoreInput]!</code> for stores.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">GraphQL</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>input ProductInput {\n    id: ID\n    name: String\n    description: String\n    price: Float\n    soldout: Soldout\n    inventory: Int\n    stores: [StoreInput]!\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0107","card":"q-graphql-022-9-final-project-reference","sec":"graphql-s018","q":"What does the final <code>resolvers.js</code> start with and export?","a":"<p>It imports <code>Widgets</code> from <code>dbConnectors</code> and exports the <code>resolvers</code> object as default.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import { Widgets } from &#x27;./dbConnectors&#x27;;\n\nconst resolvers = {\nexport default resolvers;</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0108","card":"q-graphql-022-9-final-project-reference","sec":"graphql-s018","q":"How does the final <code>updateProduct</code> resolver look?","a":"<p>It calls <code>findOneAndUpdate</code> with the filter, the input and <code>{ new: true }</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JavaScript</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>updateProduct: async ({ input }) =&gt; {\n    try {\n        const updateWidget = await Widgets.findOneAndUpdate(\n            { _id: input.id }, input, { new: true }\n        );\n        return updateWidget;\n    } catch (error) {\n        throw new Error(error);\n    }\n},</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0109","card":"q-graphql-022-9-final-project-reference","sec":"graphql-s018","q":"Which dependencies does the final <code>package.json</code> list?","a":"<p><code>casual</code>, <code>express</code>, <code>express-graphql</code>, <code>graphql</code>, <code>lodash</code>, <code>mongoose</code>, <code>nodemon</code>, <code>sequelize</code> and <code>sqlite3</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">JSON</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>&quot;dependencies&quot;: {\n    &quot;casual&quot;: &quot;^1.6.2&quot;,\n    &quot;express&quot;: &quot;^4.18.2&quot;,\n    &quot;express-graphql&quot;: &quot;^0.12.0&quot;,\n    &quot;graphql&quot;: &quot;^16.8.1&quot;,\n    &quot;lodash&quot;: &quot;^4.17.21&quot;,\n    &quot;mongoose&quot;: &quot;^8.1.1&quot;,\n    &quot;nodemon&quot;: &quot;^3.0.3&quot;,\n    &quot;sequelize&quot;: &quot;^6.35.2&quot;,\n    &quot;sqlite3&quot;: &quot;^5.1.7&quot;\n}</code></pre></div>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0110","card":"q-graphql-023-10-gotchas-and-concept-comparisons","sec":"graphql-s019","q":"What do <code>buildSchema</code>, <code>graphqlHTTP</code> and <code>rootValue</code> do?","a":"<p><code>buildSchema</code> parses a schema string (SDL) into a schema object. <code>graphqlHTTP</code> is the Express middleware that mounts the endpoint. <code>rootValue</code> is the resolver object, and resolver names must match schema field names exactly.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0111","card":"q-graphql-023-10-gotchas-and-concept-comparisons","sec":"graphql-s019","q":"<code>type</code> vs <code>input</code> in GraphQL?","a":"<p><code>type</code> is for output, <code>input</code> is for mutation arguments. Using <code>type</code> for arguments is a runtime error.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0112","card":"q-graphql-023-10-gotchas-and-concept-comparisons","sec":"graphql-s019","q":"What do <code>[Type]</code>, <code>[Type]!</code> and <code>ID!</code> mean?","a":"<p>An optional list, a mandatory list, and a mandatory scalar.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0113","card":"q-graphql-023-10-gotchas-and-concept-comparisons","sec":"graphql-s019","q":"Enum vs Boolean in GraphQL?","a":"<p>An enum is named and extensible. Switching from Boolean to enum is a breaking change.</p>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0114","card":"q-graphql-023-10-gotchas-and-concept-comparisons","sec":"graphql-s019","q":"What common errors did the GraphQL course show?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>The <code>creatProduct</code> typo: the resolver name must match the schema name or the mutation does not resolve.</li>\n  <li>Forgetting to add a new resolver to the schema's <code>Mutation</code>/<code>Query</code> type, so GraphQL does not recognize it.</li>\n  <li>Adding a field to <code>type</code> but not to <code>input</code> (or to the model/constructor).</li>\n  <li>Using <code>Widgets.remove()</code> (deprecated) instead of <code>deleteOne</code>.</li>\n  <li>Forgetting <code>{ new: true }</code> in <code>findOneAndUpdate</code>, which returns the pre-update document.</li>\n  <li>Not restarting the server or refreshing GraphiQL after schema changes.</li>\n  <li>SQLite <code>sqlite::memory:</code> data and the in-memory <code>productDatabase</code> object are lost on restart.</li>\n</ul>","hand":true},{"id":"graphql-f0115","card":"q-graphql-023-10-gotchas-and-concept-comparisons","sec":"graphql-s019","q":"Which GraphQL data is lost on server restart?","a":"<p>The in-memory <code>productDatabase</code> object and the SQLite <code>sqlite::memory:</code> data.</p>","hand":true}];
